WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.630
 Wow, this is an
excellent wine.

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:08.640
You're going to learn how
to make great buys that

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.330
taste like $100.

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.459
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:13.459 --> 00:00:16.760
The first thing you got to
do is invest in a corkscrew.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.470
[POPPING]

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:20.960
I try not to be
pretentious about wine.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:24.950
But if you want to be, I
can help you do that also.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.420
Never do this.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:27.102
Tips.

00:00:27.102 --> 00:00:28.310
You always look at the color.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.610
How to swirl the glass.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:30.770
You just go like this.

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:32.090
More descriptors.

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:32.630
Vibrant.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:33.360
Silky.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.850
There's tannin structure.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.300
That's all part of the game.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.602
But at the same time, I
want you to enjoy wine.

00:00:38.602 --> 00:00:39.102
Ah.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.120
I'm going to take
you to Tuscany.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.440
I want to teach you about the
principles of viticulture,

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.600
the balance in the
soil and microclimate,

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.865
and why great wines are great.

00:00:53.865 --> 00:00:55.110
[CLINK]

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:58.110
Because this is my home, we will
immerse ourselves in the Tuscan

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.400
winemaking history.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.740
I want to teach you how
to really taste wines.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.140
I'm using the 100-point scale.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.880
I give up to 15 points for
color, 25 points for aroma,

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.000
25 points for
structure, and finally,

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.700
35 points for the
overall quality.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:20.070
And I have a special philosophy
about food and wine pairing.

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:21.960
I like to break the rules.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.960
I don't even mind trying white
and red at the same time.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.090
And this is a way
to really increase

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:32.740
your knowledge, understanding,
and also confidence with wine.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:34.010
It's a journey.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:35.980
It's an experience.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:39.950
I'm James Suckling, and
this is my MasterClass.

